#X text 20 10 THE FEEDBACK SYNTH: 4 neurons in one [fexpr~] \, one sample at a time. \$y1[-1] .. \$y4[-1] are the four states one sample ago \, so every neuron hears every neuron (and itself) through its weights: y_i = y_i + k (-y_i + sum_j w_ij tanh(y_j) + b_i) - a CTRNN (lesson 9) with k = dt / tau. Left ear = tanh(y_1) \, right ear = tanh(y_2). A new genome: fade out \, copy it into cur\$0 \, restart from the same state ("set") \, fade in., f 170;
