#N canvas 40 60 1300 960 breed 0;
#X text 20 10 BREED (Rojas 17.1): the ratings become a roulette wheel (a card with rating r owns a slice of width r \, no ratings at all = equal slices). Child 1 is the best card \, unchanged (elitism). Every other child: spin twice for parents A and B \, take rows 1 .. cut from A and the rest from B (the cut falls between neurons only) \, then nudge each gene with probability p by a Gaussian amount of size sigma \, clipped to -4 .. 4 (weights) or -2 .. 2 (biases)., f 175;
#X obj 20 80 t b b b b b;
#X obj 20 54 r \$0-breed;
#X text 130 80 <- right to left: 1) sums 2) wheel and best 3) history 4) the children 5) they replace the parents, f 70;
